@prefix cd: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/> .
@prefix ex: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-review-complete> {
 ex:rv-n10 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-four, ex:nn-binomial-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-bin-h, ex:rv-n10-v, ex:nn-four-f, ex:rv-n10-r ; cd:narration "N10. Predict the effect of four, sixteen, fifty and two hundred independent fair signed contributions. Hold total variance fixed. Only then enable the normal reference. Finite models remain discrete; bar areas, not raw mass heights, can be compared with a density. Dominant or dependent effects need not satisfy the same limiting argument."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n10-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-signed-grown ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n10-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:nn-binomial-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n14 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-cdf-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-cdf-h, ex:rv-normal-v, ex:nn-cdf-f ; cd:narration "N14. Move one threshold and follow the density coordinate and CDF ordinate together. At 10.20 mg/L, standardized distance two gives left probability 0.977249868 and upper probability 0.022750132. Phi is an antiderivative of the standard-normal density. No elementary antiderivative exists; express it with the special error function erf after scaling the argument and applying the half-offset. erf itself is not a probability. The integral from minus infinity fixes the CDF normalization. A density height is not a probability. The finite drawing does not truncate the mathematical law."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-normal-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-normal-cdf ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n15 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-tail-scene, ex:nn-threshold-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-tail-h, ex:p1-n15-v, ex:nn-tail-f, ex:rv-normal-r ; cd:narration "N15. Ask for the upper exceedance probability before moving the threshold. The stable method can exceed 10.20 by chance in about 2.275 percent of individual results. This is neither a fault diagnosis nor a regulatory specification. Keep inverse mode off for this forward calculation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n15-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-normal-tail ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-normal-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:nn-threshold-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n16 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-ecdf-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-ecdf-h, ex:rv-n16-v, ex:rv-n16-r ; cd:narration "N16. These are the same seeded individual draws as N08, not a new fitted dataset. Change the prefix length and compare empirical steps with the full fixed model CDF. At 1,000 readings and 10.20 mg/L the empirical fraction is 0.978. Finite-sample agreement cannot prove normality."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n16-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-ecdf-start ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n16-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:nn-ecdf-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n17 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-decision-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-decision-h, ex:p1-n17-v, ex:nn-decision-f ; cd:narration "N17. Ask the inverse question: choose a one-percent upper rate. The required threshold is 10.232634787 mg/L. This per-result known-parameter calculation is not automatically calibrated for repeated monitoring or estimated model parameters."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n17-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-normal-inverse ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n19 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-means-scene, ex:nn-means-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-means-h, ex:rv-n19-v, ex:nn-means-f, ex:rv-n19-r ; cd:narration "N19. Switch random quantities from an individual reading to a mean of independent readings. Start at six, then increase n. Same concentration axis and expectation; smaller standard error. Independence supplies variance reduction, and normal individual readings supply the exact normal sampling law. Constant bias remains."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n19-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rx-means ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n19-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:nn-means-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n20 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ; dct:references ex:nn-limits-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-limits-h, ex:rv-stress-v, ex:rv-n20-c ; cd:narration "N20. Compare stable mode zero with a single outlier and acquisition-order drift. Inspect order before pooling results. These are new synthetic stress examples, not alterations to the preceding saved nitrate readings. Censoring and mixtures are further reasons that an unconditional normal model may fail."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-stress-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:v3-observation-stress ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n20-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:nn-limits-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n22 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-data, ex:lg-compare-live, ex:lg-saved ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-saved-h, ex:lg-saved-v, ex:rv-n22-r ; cd:narration "N22. Compare fictional repeat injections with separately constructed full-preparation outcomes. Their histogram shapes motivate questions about absolute and relative influences; they do not establish a population distribution from a small sample. Keep the independent preparation design visible and preserve the raw data in the extended path."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n22-info a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "What changes when each aliquot undergoes the whole preparation? Additional relative influences can create a right tail. Instrument reinjections alone are a different experiment; skewness does not prove lognormality."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n22-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n22-info ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n22-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-compare-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n23 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-product-scene, ex:lg-factor-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-factor-h, ex:rv-n23-v, ex:rv-n23-f, ex:rv-n23-r ; cd:narration "N23. Equal absolute changes and equal relative factors differ. The printed state multiplies by 1.25, then by its reciprocal 0.80: ten becomes 12.5, then ten again. Compare concentration and dimensionless natural-log-ratio views of exactly the same trajectory. Relative factors are not literal unbounded physical recoveries."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n23-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-factors ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n23-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-product ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n23-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-factor-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n25 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-transform-live, ex:lg-definition-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-definition-h, ex:rv-log-v, ex:rv-n25-f, ex:rv-n25-r ; cd:narration "N25. A normal dimensionless log ratio becomes a positive skewed concentration after exponentiation. Increase log SD while holding median fixed. The arithmetic expectation rises; symmetry is on the log scale, not on the concentration axis. The simulated process is an assumed model, not empirical validation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-log-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-log-transform ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n25-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-definition ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n25-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-transform-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n26 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-centers-scene, ex:lg-geometric-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-centers-h, ex:p1-n26-v, ex:rv-n26-f ; cd:narration "N26. The mode, median and arithmetic expectation answer different questions. At median ten and log SD 0.30 the expectation is 10.4603 ng/L. Increasing spread separates the centers. A geometric mean estimates a log-scale center under suitable assumptions, not automatically the arithmetic mass-balance expectation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n26-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-log-centers ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n26-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-centers ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n28 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-tail-scene, ex:lg-quantile-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-tail-h, ex:p1-n28-v, ex:rv-n28-f ; cd:narration "N28. First read the forward question at 15 ng/L, then the inverse question at a five-percent upper rate. Both panels are visible together. At log SD 0.30 the forward upper probability is about 0.08826 and the inverse threshold about 16.38 ng/L. Retain concentration units after back-transformation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n28-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-log-tasks ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n28-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-quantile ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n29 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-environment-live, ex:lg-checks, ex:lg-geometric-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-checks-h, ex:rv-n29-c, ex:rv-n29-r ; cd:narration "N29. Changing the sampling unit changes the population. Across-site environmental variation is not repeatability of one homogeneous preparation. Mixtures, reporting limits and censoring can distort both raw and log-scale shape. Preserve arithmetic and geometric reporting distinctions without asserting normality from positive values."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n29-info a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "A new population: concentrations across environmental sites, not reinjections of one vial. Genuine site heterogeneity, mixtures of source populations and censored low concentrations need explicit sampling and observation models. Positive values alone do not imply lognormality. Do not silently replace non-detects before fitting. Choose arithmetic expectation for additive mass balance, or a clearly described log-scale center for typical ratios."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n29-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-population-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n29-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-environment-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n30 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; dct:references ex:lg-log-variance-scene, ex:lg-bridge ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-log-variance-h, ex:rv-n30-c ; cd:narration "N30. Leave the sampling law as an open question: an estimated log-scale variance changes across samples. Announce a new IC QC study on the original concentration scale. The next section constructs the reference law before using it. The extended path retains the later exact normal-log-ratio variance identity; lognormality is not a prerequisite for the following construction."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n30-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-spread-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n31 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; dct:references ex:ic-process, ex:ic-data, ex:ic-question ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-question-h, ex:rv-n31-v ; cd:narration "N31. Announce a new fictional six-reading nitrate QC series. Repeatability, not bias, is the question. Compare with a fixed SD reference of 0.10 mg/L under normal independent readings. The CRM series will be another clearly announced study. Treat the validation SD as known for this teaching comparison; if its estimation uncertainty matters, use a different justified variance comparison. Prespecify a one-sided increased-spread alternative at five percent."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n31-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ic-process-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n32 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; dct:references ex:ic-deviations, ex:ic-spread-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-deviations-h, ex:ic-deviations-t, ex:rv-n32-f ; cd:narration "N32. Center the six QC readings at their own sample mean 10.05 mg/L, not the nominal ten. The residual sum of squares is 0.12 (mg/L) squared. Divide by five to get variance 0.024, then take the positive root to get sample SD about 0.155 mg/L. Distinguish units at every step."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n32-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ic-spread ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n34 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; dct:references ex:ix-repeat-live, ex:ic-repeated-series ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-repeated-h, ex:rv-variance-v, ex:rv-variance-r ; cd:narration "N34. Hold six readings per complete series and true SD fixed. Change simulation count or seed. A sample variance is random even under an unchanged stable method. The observed QC variance is separately marked as 0.024. The next construction explains the distribution instead of treating the histogram as a proof."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-variance-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rx-variance ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-variance-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ix-simulation ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n36 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; dct:references ex:ix-sum-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-sum-h, ex:rv-n36-v, ex:ix-sum-f ; cd:narration "N36. Change independent components from one to two to five. Squared standard-normal terms add their degrees of freedom. Independence matters; six centered residuals share an estimated mean and cannot simply be treated as six such independent terms."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n36-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-five-squares ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n41 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; dct:references ex:ix-size-scene, ex:ix-size-live, ex:ix-outlook ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-size-h, ex:p1-n41-v, ex:ix-size-f, ex:rv-variance-r ; cd:narration "N41. Compare six and thirty readings per series directly on the same variance grid while holding true precision fixed. Relative SD of the variance estimate falls from 63.2 to 26.3 percent. More Monte Carlo series only improve the picture. Larger Q means can reflect larger df, not poorer precision. A second uncertain variance motivates F; first consider a mean with an uncertain denominator."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n41-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-variance-compare ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n42 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ; dct:references ex:tf-crm-scene, ex:tf-data-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-crm-h, ex:tf-crm-c, ex:rv-n42-t ; cd:narration "N42. New fictional CRM series, retained exactly for later device A. Six readings give mean 10.10 and sample SD 0.10 mg/L. True repeatability SD is unknown. The CRM reference 10.00 has negligible uncertainty only in this teaching example. Ask whether a systematic high bias is supported before choosing the reference law."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n42-t a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-data ; cd:communicativeRole cd:TableRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasTableRow" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n43 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ; dct:references ex:tf-known-scene, ex:tf-estimated-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-known-h, ex:tf-known-f, ex:rv-n43-f ; cd:narration "N43. The numerical departure can be identical while its reference differs. Known population SD gives a normal statistic; an SD estimated from these same six results gives a Student statistic. Do not silently promote observed SD to known sigma. Repeated samples change both numerator and denominator."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n43-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-estimated ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n44 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ; dct:references ex:tf-student-live, ex:tf-denominator-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-denominator-h, ex:rv-student-v, ex:rv-n44-c ; cd:narration "N44. Repeat whole independent normal series. Each mean is divided by its own estimated SE. Small denominator estimates create heavier tails without changing the underlying individual-reading model. Start with n two, giving one Student degree of freedom, and inspect both density overlays before moving to the derivation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-student-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n44-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-denominator ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-student-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-student-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n46 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ; dct:references ex:tf-df-scene, ex:tf-df-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-df-live-h, ex:p1-n46-v, ex:rv-n46-c ; cd:narration "N46. Compare Student densities with three and twenty-nine degrees of freedom and the standard normal limit. Increasing the number of independent normal readings stabilizes the estimated denominator. Discuss shape, symmetry and tail weight, without introducing a test or an observed CRM case."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n46-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-compare ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n46-info a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "- **More measurements:** a more stable estimated denominator.\n- **More degrees of freedom:** lighter tails, closer to the normal density.\n- **Same center:** the distributions remain symmetric around zero."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n46-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n46-info ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n49 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-devices-scene, ex:tf-ratio-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-devices-h, ex:rv-n49-v, ex:rv-n49-f ; cd:narration "N49. Two fictional independent groups illustrate two sample variances. Preserve all six readings in each group. A has mean 10.10 and SD 0.10, B mean 10.00 and SD 0.30 mg/L. The descriptive B/A variance ratio is nine; do not make a population decision from it. The following simulation explains the ratio's distribution."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n49-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rx-devices ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n49-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-ratio ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n50 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-f-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-f-live-h, ex:rv-f-v ; cd:narration "N50. Equal true variances do not force equal sample estimates. Simulate independent pairs and inspect the random B/A ratio. A small denominator creates a long right tail. Equal means are not required for the variance-ratio reference. Do not infer the true ratio from the observed nine."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-f-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-f-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-f-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n52 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-f-df-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-f-df-h, ex:p1-n52-v, ex:rv-n52-c ; cd:narration "N52. The printed hypothetical design has ten B readings and six A readings, yielding ordered df nine and five for B/A. Reverse switches the ratio to its reciprocal and exchanges numerator and denominator df together. It never sorts observed variances. The original observed device data still have six per group."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n52-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-df ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n52-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-f-df ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n53 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-f-decision-scene, ex:tf-alpha-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-f-decision-h, ex:p1-n53-v, ex:rv-n53-c ; cd:narration "N53. Return to six per group, B/A and alpha 0.05. The printed plot marks both bounds and observed nine. Nine exceeds the equal-tail upper cutoff 7.1463818; two-sided p is 0.03074944. Reject equal variances conditionally on independent normal sampling. The alpha control illustrates sensitivity, not permission to select alpha after seeing data."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n53-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-f-decision ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n53-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-f-decision ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n55 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-calibration-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-calibration-h, ex:p1-n55-v ; cd:narration "N55. First inspect enlarged residuals of the linear fit on the new constructed twelve-point calibration. A systematic bend motivates considering another term. The next scene fits both nested models to these exact same observations. Lower RSS alone cannot establish that the extra term is useful."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n55-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-calibration-residuals ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-cal-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:v3-calibration-comparison ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n55-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-calibration ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n56 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-cal-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-cal-live-h, ex:rv-cal-v, ex:rv-cal-r ; cd:narration "N56. Compare both fits and their residuals without changing the observations. Read simple RSS, complex RSS and their improvement. Count the intercept: two versus three coefficients. Constructed residuals illustrate calculation but do not verify iid homoscedastic normal errors."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-cal-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-cal-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n58 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; dct:references ex:tf-assume-live, ex:tf-assumptions-scene, ex:tf-design-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-assume-live-h, ex:p1-n58-v, ex:rv-n58-c, ex:rv-n58-r ; cd:narration "N58. The printed state adds one outlier to B; the stable state and drift remain available on the same concentration scale. A nominal reference p may no longer be calibrated. One example is not a false-positive-rate study. Pairing, dependence, Welch inference about means and robust variance comparisons address different problems. Randomization and replication may be more important than changing the test name."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n58-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-stress-outlier ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n58-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-design ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n58-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-assume-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n60 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:rev-qq ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ; dct:references ex:rev-check-start, ex:rev-qq-build, ex:rev-qq-read ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-h, ex:rev-qq-read-c, ex:rev-qq-read-v, ex:rv-n60-f ; cd:narration "N60. New constructed five-reading A and B samples, not devices A and B from the variance study. Plot observed ordered readings against quantiles of a fixed normal model with mean ten and SD 0.50 mg/L. A follows the identity line; B bends. A freely fitted line would instead emphasize shape. Five points cannot establish normality."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n60-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rev-qq-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-kolmogorov-smirnov ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ; dct:references ex:rev-ks-overlay, ex:rev-ks-scale, ex:rev-ks-table-scene ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-ks-overlay-h, ex:rv-n61-v, ex:rv-n61-c, ex:rv-n61-r ; cd:narration "N61. Retain the same two samples and fixed normal CDF. KS is the maximum vertical gap, checking both sides of every empirical jump. At n five the exact two-sided 5% cutoff is 0.563275. A distance 0.144578 does not reject, B distance 0.725747 rejects. Estimated parameters require a different calibration, not the fixed-CDF table. The extended path retains the symbolic supremum definition and its complete legend."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61-info a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-n61-decision, ex:rv-n61-fitted ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61-decision a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Fixed model: compare both distances with 0.563275"@en ; cd:body "Normal mean 10 and SD 0.50 mg/L are fixed before sampling. Five independent continuously distributed measurement results give the exact two-sided 5% cutoff 0.563275. A: distance 0.144578, do not reject. B: distance 0.725747, reject. Non-rejection does not prove normality. Compare vertical gaps at both sides of every ECDF jump."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61-fitted a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "A model fitted to these data needs another reference"@en ; cd:body "If mean and SD are estimated from these measurement results, the fixed-model cutoff is no longer calibrated. Use a suitable Lilliefors calibration or parametric bootstrap refitting every replicate. Standardizing the observation axis is optional; probabilities do not change. Ties, censoring and dependence also require matching calibration."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n61-info ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rev-ks-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n61-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 5 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rev-ks-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n62 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-pearson-gof ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ; dct:references ex:rev-pearson-start, ex:rev-pearson-sum ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-pearson-start-h, ex:rv-pearson-v, ex:rv-n62-f ; cd:narration "N62. New grouped particle-count study, independent of the Q-Q and KS readings. One hundred classifications use five fixed exhaustive categories and probabilities. Expected counts ten, twenty, forty, twenty, ten; observed four, twelve, forty-four, twenty-four, sixteen. Contributions 3.6, 3.2, 0.4, 0.8, 3.6 sum to 11.6. This categorical approximation is not the exact sample-variance law."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-pearson-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rx-pearson ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n62-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-p20a-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n63 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-pearson-gof ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ; dct:references ex:rev-pearson-table-scene, ex:rev-pearson-pair ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-pearson-table-h, ex:p1-n63-v, ex:v3-n63-f, ex:rv-n63-r ; cd:narration "N63. Calculate the first contribution: four minus ten, squared and divided by ten gives 3.6. Add all five weighted discrepancies to get 11.6. No fitted category probabilities, so the fixed total leaves four df. Compare with cutoff 9.487729, p 0.020587. Compatible counts give 0.225 without changing the rule. Non-rejection cannot establish the model and rejection does not identify the cause."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n63-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-pearson-contributions ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n63-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rev-pearson-lookup ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n63-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rev-pearson-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n64 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-monte-carlo ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-mc ; dct:references ex:mc-story, ex:mc-model, ex:mc-assumptions ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:mc-story-h, ex:rv-n64-f, ex:rv-n64-c, ex:rv-n64-v ; cd:narration "N64. A new dilution study targets concentration in one collected sample, not an environmental mean. Pipette ten mL into a hundred-mL flask and use a fixed linear calibration. Nominal absorbance 0.200 gives 20.00 mg/L. Specify independent normal signal uncertainty and two uniform volume models before propagation. Real calibration and reference uncertainty are not silently included."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n64-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:mc-equation ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n64-inputs a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-n64-inputs-entry ; dct:references ex:mc-inputs ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n64-inputs-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Three independent input models, not laboratory validation"@en ; cd:body "Absorbance: normal, mean 0.200 and SD 0.003. Pipette: uniform from 9.98 to 10.02 mL. Flask: uniform from 99.92 to 100.08 mL. Calibration slope 0.095 L/mg and intercept 0.010 stay fixed. The normal signal model has real-line support, with negligible negative tail here. Calibration uncertainty, recovery and input dependence are not included."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n64-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n64-inputs ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n64-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:al-process-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n65 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-monte-carlo ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-mc ; dct:references ex:mc-transform, ex:mc-trial, ex:mc-live ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:mc-trial-h, ex:p1-n65-v, ex:rv-n65-f, ex:rv-mc-r ; cd:narration "N65. The initial and printed state is one trial: inspect all three uniforms, transformed signal and volumes, then the resulting concentration. Only afterward increase repetitions or move to the ten-thousand-result next scene. Quantile transforms supply draws from the stated input models. More trials reduce numerical simulation error, not physical measurement uncertainty. R remains an optional replay."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:p1-n65-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:p1-dilution-trial ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-mc-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:rx-dilution ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n65-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:mc-inverse ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-mc-r a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:mc-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:optionalCode true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n66 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-monte-carlo ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-mc ; dct:references ex:mc-result, ex:mc-scope ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:mc-result-h, ex:rv-mc-v, ex:rv-n66-c, ex:rv-mc-r ; cd:narration "N66. Reset to ten thousand and seed 20261101. Mean 19.9986223648564, SD 0.31674478361247, central type-seven interval 19.37110491120053 to 20.62749774955301 mg/L. Compare absorbance-only, volumes-only and combined inputs. This interval describes model-propagated concentration uncertainty, not automatically a confidence interval for a true mean or empirical validation of the laboratory process."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:rv-n66-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:mc-limits ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

